-- title:
--   Vertical order of j at the cusp section's special point
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and write $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ with $X$ integral. The data are: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ together with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the generic fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$ compatible with the structure maps; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose associated place is the cusp `cuspInftyFull N`; a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of the generic fibre that is a section over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q}$, whose first projection is $\varepsilon_\infty$ base-changed to $\mathbb{Q}$, and which corresponds to $x_0$ under $e_0^{-1}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-fibre, Galois-equivariance of its point–place bijection for the `arithmeticGalois` action, and compatibility of its places with those of $M_0$ under restriction along $F_N \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} F_N \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N`; for every valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit, a lift $\rho_A : R \to A$ of the structure map, a curve model of `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A) N` isomorphic over the residue field to the corresponding fibre, and, when that residue field is algebraically closed, a degree-preserving reduction map $r$ on places satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` and compatible with reduction of points. Finally let $s$ be a closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ such that the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$. The conclusion: there are an integer $n$ and elements $a, b$ of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\varepsilon_\infty(s)}$, neither lying in the ideal generated by the germ of $p$ there, such that, after specialisation to the stalk at the generic cusp, transport by the stalk map of $e_0$ followed by the first projection, passage to the function field of $M_0.C$ and identification with `modularFunctionFieldFull N` inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, the resulting Laurent series satisfy $\mathrm{image}(a) = j(q)\, p^{\,n}\, \mathrm{image}(b)$.
--
--   This expresses that the modular function $j$ has a well-defined order $n$ along the special fibre at the special point of the cusp section of an integral proper smooth $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of $X_0(N)$, written as $j = p^{n} a/b$ with germs $a,b$ prime to $p$ in the local ring there. It feeds the statement in which this order is shown to vanish, so that $j$ is a unit times a ratio of germs prime to $p$ at the cusp.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_int_notMem_span_germ_and_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_zpow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero.lean

